@* The document shell for the admin UI.
   <para>
   It lives in the host project rather than in DailyMusings.Admin, and that placement is load-bearing rather than
   cosmetic: the framework only publishes its _framework assets — including blazor.web.js, the script that
   establishes the Blazor circuit — when the *host* project is itself a Razor project. With the shell in the class
   library the host contained no Razor component at all, so nothing ever published that script: the pages rendered
   and every button on them silently did nothing, while plain form posts (sign-in, sign-out) kept working.
   </para>
   <para>
   Verified by publishing the project with and without a component in it: the script appears under
   wwwroot/_framework only in the former. deploy/Dockerfile asserts it is present so this cannot regress silently.
   </para>
   <para>
   Everything else — pages, layouts, routing, its own imports — stays in the class library, which is what keeps the
   admin surface separate from the host. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="zh-CN">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>每日随想 · 管理</title>
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/DailyMusings.Admin/admin.css?v=20260925-2" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    @* Static SSR for the shell: the forms post to real endpoints and need the HTTP request context, while the
       data pages opt into interactivity themselves. *@
    <Routes />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
